WEBVTT

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:02.940
It's the Duel Carnival Final!

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:05.400
<i>I started my Duel with Tron in the Sphere Field.</i>

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:09.360
<i>The both of us have Summoned three Numbers, and the real fight begins now!</i>

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:11.400
<i>I won't allow myself to lose!</i>

00:00:11.940 --> 00:00:13.780
<i>I'm gonna bring it to 'im!</i>

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.000
To think you <i>also</i> called out three...

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:23.960
Seems you have some luck on your side.

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:27.460
It wasn't luck!
 This is just how skilled I am!

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:31.300
We can win with this battle formation!
 Pass right through him, Yuma!

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:32.460
Yeah!

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:35.620
I activate Leviath Dragon's effect!

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:41.590
I detach one of its Overlay Units to increase its Attack Power by 500 points!

00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:44.100
Go, Leviath Dragon!

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:45.980
Attack Shining White Knight Illuminator!

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:48.560
Vice Stream!

00:00:57.380 --> 00:01:02.430
Once again! Go on, Aspiring Emperor - Hope!

00:01:02.430 --> 00:01:04.730
Attack Genome Heriter!

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:09.970
Hope Sword Slash!

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:22.930
But it's hardly anything to get too excited about.

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:28.190
I still have the 3000 Attack Power Acid Golem on my field!

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:33.600
I'm not done! I activate a Magic from my hand!

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:36.320
Xyz Triangle Force!

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:41.340
When I have three or more Xyz Monsters on my field,

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:44.340
I can destroy one card on my opponent's field!

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:50.040
Go! Destroy Acid Golem!

00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:59.590
So you had that card in reserve, did you?

00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:03.850
Tron! Now I've defeated all your Numbers!

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:07.460
I'm starting to think it'll actually happen!

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:09.730
Tron doesn't have any set cards or even a hand.

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:13.150
If he doesn't Summon a Monster on his next turn...

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:15.030
Yuma's gonna win!

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:16.740
Go for it, Yuma!

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:24.330
I end my turn now!
 So bring it to me!

00:02:25.950 --> 00:02:30.120
I'm starting to think you <i>really</i> believe you can defeat me.

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:34.210
Of course I do! For both III and Kaito,

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:36.220
I'm definitely gonna beat you!

00:02:36.220 --> 00:02:39.430
You have three Numbers on your field.

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:43.900
It seems the battlefield is finally ready for me to get serious.

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:45.810
Wh-What?

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:48.450
This is my Destiny Draw!

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:50.850
I'm gonna bring it to 'im!

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.270
Just kidding.

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:59.570
Here I go now! I activate the effect of the Heraldic Beast Unicorn in my Graveyard!

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:02.820
By Banishing this card from the Graveyard,

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:06.540
I can negate the effect of one Xyz Monster in the Graveyard...

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:08.540
...in order to Special Summon it!

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:12.420
Show yourself, Shining White Knight Illuminator!

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:19.080
Then I activate the effect of the other Heraldic Beast Unicorn in the Graveyard!

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:23.180
I'll Special Summon the Genome Heriter in my Graveyard the same way!

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:28.730
It's no use Summoning that Monster!

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:31.600
My Monsters have the higher Attack Points!

00:03:31.710 --> 00:03:37.570
No, he didn't bring back the Monsters so he could attack with them.

00:03:37.570 --> 00:03:38.230
Huh?

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:45.070
If attacking was his goal, he would have revived the 3000 Attack Power Acid Golem.

00:03:45.110 --> 00:03:50.200
I activate the Magic Card, Reborn Medallion, from my hand!

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:55.250
This card revives a Level Four or lower Heraldic Beast from my Graveyard!

00:03:56.470 --> 00:04:00.380
Revive! Heraldic Beast Bernard's Falcon!

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:12.230
I activate Bernard's Falcon's effect!

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:15.270
When this card appears on the field,

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:20.080
it can change all the Monsters on my field to the same level.

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:27.160
He's changing the levels of his Xyz Monsters?!

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:31.540
Now he has three Level Four Monsters on his field!

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:32.120
He can't be...

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:38.000
I Overlay Illuminator, Genome Heriter, and Bernard's Falcon!

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:50.100
I build the Overlay Network using these three Monsters!

00:04:50.470 --> 00:04:52.020
Xyz Summon!

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:55.440
Show yourself, Number 69!

00:04:56.100 --> 00:05:00.230
Allow me to show you my <i>real</i> trump card!

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:07.660
God Medallion - Coat of Arms!

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:15.000
So that Number has finally appeared...

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:24.300
That's the Number that made quick work of Neo Galaxy-Eyes.

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:25.130
Yuma!

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:35.810
This is the Number that makes up the very essence of Tron's desire for revenge.

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:43.030
How it hurts.

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:46.860
Hatred pours out from within me and suffocates me!

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:48.950
I no longer need this mask.

00:05:49.160 --> 00:05:53.200
After all, my Duel with you two will be the last one.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:56.370
When it's all over, my memories...

00:05:56.370 --> 00:06:00.170
...rather, <i>anything and everything</i>, will be stolen away.

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:03.630
I'll make an <i>exception</i> and <i>show you</i>...

00:06:03.630 --> 00:06:05.510
...my true form!

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:12.300
Th-That is...

00:06:15.950 --> 00:06:17.270
Byron...

00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:28.790
<i>Advance, advance, beyond the limits of your strength</i>

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:34.130
<i>Come along with me and burn our flame of life</i>

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:50.980
<i>Hey, my friends, what scenery do you suppose</i>

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:56.780
<i>awaits us on the other side of this hill?</i>

00:06:57.570 --> 00:07:01.370
<i>Hey, my friends, let's climb it together</i>

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:07.410
<i>It's too soon for us to turn back now</i>

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:12.500
<i>The time has come to combine
 together the power dwelling inside me</i>

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:18.050
<i>Gotta release my Soul Drive</i>

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:23.850
<i>Advance, advance, beyond the limits of your strength</i>

00:07:24.060 --> 00:07:28.890
<i>Come along with me and burn our flame of life</i>

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:34.360
<i>Keep running, keep running, until you get there</i>

00:07:34.690 --> 00:07:40.030
<i>Once again, once again, keep those challenges coming</i>

00:07:41.110 --> 00:07:46.200
<i>My friends, keep on living in the here and now</i>

00:07:46.490 --> 00:07:52.290
<i>Keep pressing onward together no matter what happens</i>

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:05.630
H-His face...

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:10.420
Yes... While I wandered the threshold between the Parallel Worlds,

00:08:08.590 --> 00:08:13.260
"Number 66: The Terrifying Duel!
 Arise, Hero of Bond ZEXAL!"

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:13.680
I ended up with the form you see before you.

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:20.730
A heart of revenge is the only thing
 that remains in this body of mine!

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:26.690
Tron... Does this mean your true form is a being not of this human planet?!

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:33.950
That AR is so freakin' cool!

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:35.700
I can't believe he even changed his appearance!

00:08:35.700 --> 00:08:37.240
That's the Final for you!

00:08:37.370 --> 00:08:40.160
They're wrong! That's no AR!

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:43.210
To summarize, that's his true form!

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:45.000
Yuma, run away...!

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:47.590
Guys, keep it together!

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:51.670
Who's going to root for Yuma if we don't?!

00:08:51.670 --> 00:08:54.550
Go, Yuma!

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:59.260
Yuma! Astral! Have a look at my power!

00:08:59.890 --> 00:09:03.520
This is the ultimate Number I've gotten my hands on!

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:06.350
And this guy has a very <i>special </i>effect.

00:09:07.690 --> 00:09:11.480
Coat of Arms can't be destroyed by Card Effects,

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:15.700
and he negates the effects of <i>all</i> Monsters on the field!

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:18.950
He can then make their effects his own!

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:22.160
He can make the effects of other Monsters his own?!

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:25.500
That's right. No matter what Monster it may be,

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:28.210
they are completely helpless before Coat of Arms!

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:33.170
I'll show you that friendship and hope mean <i>nothing</i>!

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:35.930
Coat of Arms' effect activates!

00:09:35.930 --> 00:09:38.300
God Medallion Hand!

00:09:57.860 --> 00:10:01.580
Their Monster Effects were stolen!

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:04.830
Well, I guess I'll use them right away.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:07.870
I activate Coat of Arm's effect!

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:12.840
By detaching one Overlay Unit, I can use the stolen Leviath Dragon's effect!

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:17.720
Meaning Coat of Arm's Attack Power goes up 500 points!

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:22.140
Then I activate the effect of the Heraldic Beast Leo from my Graveyard!

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:25.180
When one of my Monster's Attack Power changes,

00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:28.850
I can Banish this card and take the same amount of added Attack Power

00:10:28.850 --> 00:10:32.400
and decrease the Attack Power of one of my opponent's Monsters!

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:34.860
Leviath Dragon's Attack Power was...!

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:40.030
Now, go do it! Bury Leviath Dragon!

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:43.410
Take this! God Rage!

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:04.180
The power of his Number is incredible.

00:11:04.470 --> 00:11:06.470
Very interesting, Byron.

00:11:06.470 --> 00:11:09.850
To think you would go this far to realize your desire for revenge!

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:11.690
How interesting!

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:14.650
A-Are you all right, Yuma?

00:11:14.650 --> 00:11:16.650
Yeah, I'm hanging in there.

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:17.860
Hanging in there?

00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:21.360
It's about time you give up.

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:27.370
Unlike the useless III, IV, and V, I'm invincible.

00:11:27.370 --> 00:11:32.880
That's right. You can say this Coat of Arms represents the difference in strength between parent and child!

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:35.000
Between parent and child, huh?\

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:38.670
It <i>is</i> true that Monster is <i>exactly</i> like you!

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:39.920
<i>What</i>?

00:11:40.670 --> 00:11:42.510
I understand completely now!

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:45.890
For III, IV, and even V...

00:11:46.180 --> 00:11:50.060
They were great people! They were splendid!

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:51.980
They frantically supported you!

00:11:52.690 --> 00:11:56.940
To the very end, all of them were worried about you!

00:11:57.190 --> 00:11:59.780
And yet, why do such nice guys...

00:12:00.690 --> 00:12:04.660
...have to throw everything away for someone like you?!

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:09.620
It's the natural thing for a parent and child to do for each other!

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:10.960
But that isn't right!

00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:13.500
They believed in you!

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:15.880
That you'd return to them some day!

00:12:15.880 --> 00:12:17.250
Yuma...

00:12:17.250 --> 00:12:22.300
But why couldn't you be a little nicer to them after returning?!

00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:26.680
Why'd you start pushing them to a dead end for something as boring as revenge?!

00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:31.680
A child like you couldn't possibly understand...!

00:12:31.680 --> 00:12:33.390
I <i>do</i> understand!

00:12:33.690 --> 00:12:38.940
I understand how lonely it feels when your father goes missing!

00:12:38.940 --> 00:12:42.900
Every one of them have been lonely since you went missing!

00:12:45.110 --> 00:12:48.950
And they still gave it their best despite the tears it brought them!

00:12:49.740 --> 00:12:52.540
Shut up! I won't let you sit here and...

00:12:54.920 --> 00:12:56.000
<i>III...</i>

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:57.460
<i>IV...</i>

00:12:58.630 --> 00:12:59.460
<i>V...</i>

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:02.510
<i>Memories... of my family.</i>

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:08.680
<i>All of it... All of it, along with my face...</i>

00:13:10.970 --> 00:13:13.640
I won't give up on this Duel!

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:19.610
Until I deliver to you what they've all entrusted me with,

00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:21.650
I won't ever give up!

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:26.740
Fine then. I'll let you fall prey to my Coat of Arms instantly.

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:28.870
I'll end my turn!

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:31.370
Let's go, Astral!

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:33.040
Yuma...

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:38.250
ZEXAL. If we want to beat him, we have no choice but to use ZEXAL.

00:13:38.500 --> 00:13:45.470
Yuma, this Sphere Field is a psuedo-space created to mimic the Parallel Worlds.

00:13:45.470 --> 00:13:47.680
It's the same as the Empreror's Key.

00:13:47.890 --> 00:13:50.140
We can use ZEXAL here.

00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:53.560
However, there are countless people watching this Duel.

00:13:53.560 --> 00:13:55.480
It doesn't matter what they think!

00:13:55.480 --> 00:13:58.190
As long as it lets me deliver their feelings to him.

00:13:58.520 --> 00:14:01.520
Let's do it, Astral!

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:05.320
Come along with me, Yuma!

00:14:05.690 --> 00:14:08.700
I'm gonna bring it to 'em!

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:09.530
I will...

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:11.410
...along with me!

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:13.080
Overlay!

00:14:30.970 --> 00:14:37.270
In the moment two distant souls cross over, the legendary power will come forth!

00:14:42.520 --> 00:14:44.940
Xyz Change!

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:46.940
ZEXAL!

00:14:55.240 --> 00:14:56.870
D-Did he say ZEXAL...?

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:01.920
- What the heck is that?
 - He transformed!

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:10.220
That's the power of Yuma and Astral's bond!

00:15:10.630 --> 00:15:13.930
W-Why's he doing it when everyone's watching?

00:15:14.390 --> 00:15:16.600
To summarize, I wonder myself...

00:15:16.770 --> 00:15:17.850
C-Cat...

00:15:18.180 --> 00:15:20.480
Maybe they all think it's just AR.

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:24.150
Wow, Yuma looks really cool right now!

00:15:24.400 --> 00:15:26.280
He looks like a real hero, doesn't he?

00:15:26.280 --> 00:15:27.570
I know, right!

00:15:27.940 --> 00:15:29.190
He's so cool!

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:33.700
Yeah! That's a genuine hero!

00:15:34.950 --> 00:15:37.290
Hey, Tokunosuke, stop that!

00:15:37.740 --> 00:15:42.080
That's ZEXAL! It's our hero who protects Heartland!

00:15:42.370 --> 00:15:45.130
And his name's ZEXAL, or not!

00:15:45.130 --> 00:15:46.170
ZEXALornot?

00:15:46.170 --> 00:15:47.380
ZEXALornot?

00:15:47.550 --> 00:15:49.590
Ah! So he's called ZEXALornot?!

00:15:49.590 --> 00:15:50.670
I like it!

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:51.760
ZEXALornot!

00:15:52.010 --> 00:15:54.680
Um, no... When I said "or not"...

00:15:54.680 --> 00:16:03.730
ZEXALornot! ZEXAlornot! ZEXALornot!

00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:10.440
W-We might... have a huge misunderstanding
 on our hands here... or not.

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:17.200
ZEXALornot! ZEXALornot! ZEXALornot!

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:19.240
Well... Guess it's okay.

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:25.790
Amazing... So many people are cheering for Yuma and Astral.

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:38.390
ZEXALornot! ZEXALornot! ZEXALornot!

00:16:38.390 --> 00:16:42.640
I can't believe you were hiding that combination ability of yours this whole time.

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:45.020
Did they say "ZEXALornot"...?

00:16:45.520 --> 00:16:48.900
Don't worry about the tiny details.
 Just focus on the Duel.

00:16:48.900 --> 00:16:51.320
R-Right... I know.

00:16:51.780 --> 00:16:53.860
My turn! Draw!

00:16:55.820 --> 00:16:58.200
Yuma! Let's Chaos Xyz Change!

00:16:58.580 --> 00:17:04.290
Right! I use Aspiring Emperor - Hope as Xyz Material in order to Xyz Change!

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:09.090
Show yourself, Chaos Number 39!

00:17:12.510 --> 00:17:14.680
Aspiring Emperor - Hope Ray!

00:17:24.690 --> 00:17:27.350
So Aspiring Emperor - Hope Ray makes an appearance.

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:31.900
But it's useless. I activate Coat of Arm's effect!

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:34.240
God Medallion Hand!

00:17:35.900 --> 00:17:39.320
Hope Ray, I'll steal all of your Monster Effects!

00:17:39.620 --> 00:17:42.370
I won't let you! I activate a Magic Card!

00:17:42.370 --> 00:17:43.290
Seven Store!

00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:49.500
By releasing one of our Xyz Monsters, Seven Store allows us to draw another card!

00:17:49.500 --> 00:17:52.000
I select Terror-byte!

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:56.340
And when the Monster is released, for the number of Overlay Units it had,

00:17:57.380 --> 00:18:00.260
I can draw another card!

00:18:01.720 --> 00:18:04.350
Terror-byte had two Overlay Units attached to it.

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:06.980
So I can now draw three times!

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:09.940
Everything is inevitable in the strongest Duelist's Dueling!

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:13.400
Even the cards they draw can be created by the Duelist!

00:18:13.690 --> 00:18:15.900
Let's go, Astral!

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:18.240
All light, give me power!

00:18:18.240 --> 00:18:21.410
Gather into my right hand and illuminate a path toward hope!

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:27.410
Shining Draw!

00:18:28.960 --> 00:18:30.880
The ZEXAL Weapon's here!

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:35.840
Coat of Arms can negate the effects of its opponent's Monsters and absorb them.

00:18:35.840 --> 00:18:39.550
But you can't steal the effect of 
the ZEXAL Weapon treated as an Equip!

00:18:39.890 --> 00:18:42.760
I see. Very well thought out.

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:47.230
I equip ZEXAL Weapon - Lightning Blade!

00:18:47.980 --> 00:18:51.230
This ZEXAL Weapon does not need to be Summoned on the field.

00:18:51.230 --> 00:18:56.150
Instead it can be directly equipped to Hope Ray, and it gains 1200 Attack Points!

00:18:56.150 --> 00:18:59.280
Then, when this card is equipped,

00:18:59.570 --> 00:19:03.370
Magic and Trap Cards we control cannot be destroyed!

00:19:12.920 --> 00:19:14.750
Go, Hope Ray!

00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:17.920
Among the effects snatched by Coat of Arms,

00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:19.930
it doesn't have the power to evade this one!

00:19:21.180 --> 00:19:23.930
Hope Sword Lightning Blade!

00:19:25.560 --> 00:19:27.180
You're mine!

00:19:27.600 --> 00:19:31.810
That's it... I've been waiting for this attack!

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:34.270
I activate Coat of Arm's effect!

00:19:34.730 --> 00:19:37.190
When the opponent attacks,

00:19:37.190 --> 00:19:39.740
by detaching one Overlay Unit,

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:42.410
this card can destroy one card on the field!

00:19:42.410 --> 00:19:45.990
I select Aspiring Emperor - Hppe Ray and destroy it!

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:46.740
What?!

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:49.580
Allow me to show you...

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:53.830
<i>...the </i>original <i>power of the god!</i>

00:19:54.210 --> 00:19:56.710
Go, Coat of Arms!

00:19:56.710 --> 00:19:59.300
God Slaughter!

00:20:06.390 --> 00:20:09.220
I activate the effect of Lightning Blade!

00:20:09.220 --> 00:20:12.270
When the Monster equipped with it is destroyed in battle,

00:20:12.270 --> 00:20:16.900
I can return ZEXAL Weapon to my hand
 in order to negate its destruction!

00:20:22.990 --> 00:20:24.490
More of your tricks.

00:20:24.700 --> 00:20:27.120
But the battle still continues, you know.

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:29.830
Either way, your little hope play ends here!

00:20:30.200 --> 00:20:32.910
Take him down, Coat of Arms!

00:20:32.910 --> 00:20:36.040
Crush Hope Way into nothing!

00:20:36.790 --> 00:20:39.670
I activate Rescueleton Pig’s effect from my Graveyard!

00:20:39.670 --> 00:20:41.170
From the Graveyard?!

00:20:41.170 --> 00:20:43.880
When a Monster on our field would be destroyed,

00:20:43.880 --> 00:20:46.600
by Banishing Rescueleton Pig from the Graveyard,

00:20:46.600 --> 00:20:51.060
it negates the destruction and makes the damage zero!


00:21:11.040 --> 00:21:13.290
You saved me, Rescueleton!

00:21:14.370 --> 00:21:16.040
Stop fooling around!

00:21:16.040 --> 00:21:18.880
I can't believe you had that Monster set up in your Graveyard.

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:23.380
I equip Hope Ray once again with ZEXAL Xyz Change- Weapon Change!

00:21:36.100 --> 00:21:39.270
I set one card face-down and end my turn!

00:21:44.900 --> 00:21:48.820
You sure are persistent. I expected no less for Kazuma's son.

00:21:49.030 --> 00:21:51.740
You're the splitting image of that dull man.

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:54.250
I won't ever give up!

00:21:54.250 --> 00:21:59.330
Tron! I swear to collect everyone's feelings and send them to you!

00:22:10.350 --> 00:22:15.520
<i>We stand tall, until we have victory in our grasp</i>

00:22:15.770 --> 00:22:21.150
<i>Move on ahead, speeding up our throbbing beats</i>

00:22:26.780 --> 00:22:31.830
<i>Listen boys and girls, here's the secret to boys and girls like you</i>

00:22:32.200 --> 00:22:36.080
<i>You're really just so spontaneous, wild as can be</i>

00:22:36.080 --> 00:22:37.370
<i>I bet you didn't know?</i>

00:22:37.620 --> 00:22:40.080
<i>You might be a handful, but what's wrong with that?</i>

00:22:40.250 --> 00:22:42.710
<i>Be up to no good, but learn for real</i>

00:22:42.880 --> 00:22:47.920
<i>Go the unpredictable route and shuffle your cards with a goal in mind</i>

00:22:48.090 --> 00:22:53.260
<i>Whenever you feel like you've lost your way, just take a minute to close your eyes...</i>

00:22:53.390 --> 00:22:58.890
<i>Shout "stop!" with all you've got, and there's your boundary line.</i>

00:23:00.270 --> 00:23:05.400
<i>We stand tall, until we have victory in our grasp</i>

00:23:05.570 --> 00:23:10.860
<i>We won't just stop here, not when we don't want to have any regrets.</i>

00:23:11.030 --> 00:23:16.120
<i>Even if we get hurt, we can't just hesitate now</i>

00:23:16.370 --> 00:23:21.750
<i>We won't just give up, not when our future's a lot brighter than our today</i>

00:23:21.750 --> 00:23:26.960
<i>Seriousness... It'll only make us keep fighting even harder</i>

00:23:27.170 --> 00:23:32.470
<i>We'll always get as fascinated as we want, and we'll fight on every day</i>

00:23:40.640 --> 00:23:46.980
In the Final of the W.D.C., 
this prolonged battle is finally about to end!

00:23:46.980 --> 00:23:51.030
And the true goal of the Sphere Field is finally revealed!

00:23:51.030 --> 00:23:54.780
Yuma, we can't allow ourselves to lose this battle!

00:23:54.780 --> 00:23:56.200
The ZEXAL Weapon was...!

00:23:56.200 --> 00:23:59.120
Everything rides on this final draw!

00:23:59.120 --> 00:24:02.290
Take our all-new attack!

00:24:02.290 --> 00:24:04.500
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal!

00:24:04.500 --> 00:24:07.420
"Believe in Victory! The Final Shining Draw!"

00:24:07.420 --> 00:24:09.420
What is going on?!

00:24:10.800 --> 00:24:13.510
Just when we finally reveal our cool-looking form,

00:24:13.550 --> 00:24:15.800
why'd Tokunosuke have to go name it ZEXALornot?!

00:24:15.970 --> 00:24:18.180
The Warrior of Love and Justice, ZEXALornot.

00:24:18.680 --> 00:24:21.230
The Warrior of Victory and Courage, ZEXALornot.

00:24:22.600 --> 00:24:24.310
Hey, you shouldn't like it!
